id: pm-geywoc
title: Prevent Sentry command context from recording positional content and option values
description: "sentrySetCommandContext currently preserves every non-option argument verbatim, including free text and space-separated option values. Broader successful-command tracing must use safe argument structure and streamed-span/log scrubbing through the existing policy instead of collecting private item content."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: bugfix,observability,privacy,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-13T04:41:25.527Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T10:21:56.600Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T10:21:55.627Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T10:21:55.627Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Positional content and separate option values never enter Sentry context or breadcrumbs; streamed spans and logs scrub sensitive data before export; independent negative controls fail before the fix and pass after; existing error classification and consent remain intact.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Redact every argument slot, deny automatic sensitive collection, scrub complete spans and links plus logs, and consume complete quoted assignment values through escaped delimiters or incomplete input."
expected_result: Private argument content and quoted sensitive-value suffixes never enter diagnostic exports; unconsented command spans remain absent.
actual_result: "Independent argument, span-link, existing-client and quoted-value negatives fail before their fixes and pass afterward;90 linked Sentry tests, full10377-test exact100/100/100/100 coverage, typecheck, ESLint and final9-package Node/Bun/npx/bunx workflows pass."
